module gunbc.memory_cgroup_binding_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// THE HAND-ITEM DELTA IS ENUMERATED RATHER THAN COUNTED FROM WHAT WAS TOUCHED, by the method
// gunbc.whole_corpus_compile_admission records having got wrong twice. Fifteen declarations:
// the two constants naming the request variable and the leaf, the refusal-cause, request and
// decision coproducts, the pure decision, its two renderings, the machine-memory and
// resident-size readers, the leaf probe and its unwind, and the one impure function that
// performs the write. The request coproduct and the resident-size reader arrived with review
// 5117628699: the first so that an unreadable request is a refusal rather than silence, the
// second so that a bound at or below what the process already holds is refused before it can be
// fatal. The claim_executor call site adds no declaration --
// it is statements at the head of an existing fn, so its disposition is
// ExistingSeedItemModified and listing it would net a modification into an addition.
data memory_cgroup_binding_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "BIND_MEMORY_CGROUP_ENV", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "BIND_MEMORY_CGROUP_LEAF", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "CgroupBindRefusalCause", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "CgroupBindRequest", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "CgroupBindDecision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "cgroup_bind_decision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "cgroup_bind_refusal_cause_text", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "cgroup_bind_refusal_diagnostic", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "cgroup_bind_note", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "machine_memory_total_bytes", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "self_resident_bytes", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "cgroup_leaf_create", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "cgroup_leaf_remove_if_created", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "cgroup_memory_controller_available", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.memory_governor", decl_name: "apply_memory_cgroup_bind", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "WHY RUST IS STILL NEEDED, and it is the same bootstrap constraint the three sibling host-budget mirrors give rather than ordinary seed-shrink debt: this runs BEFORE any .dag value could exist, because it decides the memory limit the resolve of the corpus will run under. A limit obtained by resolving the corpus would be acquired after the allocations it was meant to bound. gunbc.memory_cgroup_binding is the authority and this is its realization; the pure decision is a parameter-for-parameter mirror so every discriminating case stays reachable from a test on a machine that has none of those states.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing admits a change by PURPOSE. The instrument this restores is the generated-artifact adjudication over both declared populations -- a self-host instrument -- which on the remote-execution route could not execute at all, because that action runs in the cgroup2 root where no memory.max exists and gunbc.host_budget_source correctly refuses. This is defect repair on the self-host path, not growth of the seed for its own sake.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete these declarations and this row when the v2 emit of the stage0 host-budget readers lands -- the same emit gunbc.host_budget_source and gunbc.typed_module_cache_capacity name as the dissolution of their own mirrors -- and that emit must be SUFFICIENT FOR producing the bind decision and its realization from gunbc.memory_cgroup_binding, not merely for the budget READ beside it. An emit that projected only the read would leave this write hand-authored and the row would be retired while the capability it names stayed dead.",
  current_boundary: "The bind is OPT-IN and reads its own variable: nothing acquires a limit it did not request, and GUNBC_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES is untouched in meaning or effect. A process already bound by a cgroup is never written to and takes the unnecessary arm, which is the arm every self-hosted CI runner takes. The only writing arm requires a request, no existing observation, an available memory controller, a creatable leaf, and a readable machine size strictly larger than the bound; every other combination refuses with a typed, located cause and the executor exits nonzero rather than proceeding unbounded. The bind supplies no number to any consumer -- the budget is still read afterwards through gunbc.host_budget_source's ordinary cgroup walk -- and it disarms no refusal: the stall verdict and the whole-corpus admission both keep their subjects and can still fire against the bound that was created."
}
